 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_232c230b9694481440248b0cad14c224" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_6eb0aa5856a9193a14206a6290b33d18" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_fded77b753796d5010e4a105f352bf52" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_4596b7ba0ec93a207e32b5f2d9324365" />
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Arachidonate 5-lipoxygenase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_ALOX5_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P09917" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">LOX5_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">LOG5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">5-LO</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ALOX5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.13.11.34</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">5-lipoxygenase</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_240</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_000689</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_01065_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the first step in leukotriene biosynthesis,and thereby plays a role in inflammatory processes.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:21233389}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=(5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z)-eicosatetraenoate + O2 = H2O +leukotriene A4; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:32307, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377,ChEBI:CHEBI:15379, ChEBI:CHEBI:32395, ChEBI:CHEBI:57463;EC=1.13.11.34; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:21233389};COFACTOR:Name=Fe cation; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:24875;Evidence={ECO:0000255|PROSITE-ProRule:PRU00726,ECO:0000269|PubMed:21233389};Note=Binds 1 Fe cation per subunit. {ECO:0000255|PROSITE-ProRule:PRU00726, ECO:0000269|PubMed:21233389};COFACTOR:Name=Ca(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:29108; Evidence={ECO:0000250};Note=Binds 2 calcium ions per subunit. {ECO:0000250};PATHWAY: Lipid metabolism; leukotriene A4 biosynthesis.SUBUNIT: Interacts with ALOX5AP and LTC4S. Interacts with COTL1,the interaction is required for stability and efficient catalyticactivity. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:19233132,ECO:0000269|PubMed:19807693, ECO:0000269|PubMed:21233389}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasm. Nucleus matrix. Nucleus membrane;Peripheral membrane protein. Note=Shuttles between cytoplasm andnucleus. Found exclusively in the nucleus, when phosphorylated onSer-272. Calcium binding promotes translocation from the cytosoland the nuclear matrix to the nuclear envelope and membraneassociation.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=5;Comment=Additional isoforms seem to exist.;Name=1;IsoId=P09917-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2; Synonyms=Delta-13;IsoId=P09917-2; Sequence=VSP_046998;Name=3; Synonyms=delta-p10;IsoId=P09917-3; Sequence=VSP_053534;Name=4; Synonyms=delta-10-13;IsoId=P09917-4; Sequence=VSP_053535, VSP_053537;Name=5; Synonyms=alpha-10;IsoId=P09917-5; Sequence=VSP_053536;PTM: Serine phosphorylation by MAPKAPK2 is stimulated byarachidonic acid. Phosphorylation on Ser-523 by PKA has aninhibitory effect. Phosphorylation on Ser-272 prevents export fromthe nucleus. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:11844797,ECO:0000269|PubMed:15280375, ECO:0000269|PubMed:18978352}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the lipoxygenase family. {ECO:0000305}.WEB RESOURCE: Name=Atlas of Genetics and Cytogenetics in Oncologyand Haematology;URL=&quot;http://atlasgeneticsoncology.org/Genes/ALOX5ID42985ch10q11.html&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">LOX5_HUMAN Reviewed; 674 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference77487</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.phosphosite.org/phosphosite.owl#po_3884</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_P09917_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_dip_DIP-30950N_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_240</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

