toward 12(13)-epoxy-(9Z)-octadecenoate (isoform CYP4F3A) {ECO:0000269|PubMed:15145985};Vmax=3.93 nmol/min/nmol enzyme toward 12(13)-epoxy-(9Z)-octadecenoate (isoform CYP4F3B) {ECO:0000269|PubMed:15145985};Vmax=5.0 pmol/min/pmol enzyme toward docosanoate (isoformCYP4F3B) {ECO:0000269|PubMed:16547005};Vmax=9.8 pmol/min/pmol enzyme toward tetracosanoate (isoformCYP4F3B) {ECO:0000269|PubMed:16547005};Vmax=2.2 pmol/min/pmol enzyme toward hexacosanoate (isoformCYP4F3B) {ECO:0000269|PubMed:16547005};Vmax=0.2 pmol/min/pmol enzyme toward 22-hydroxydocosanoate(isoform CYP4F3A) {ECO:0000269|PubMed:18182499};Vmax=0.3 pmol/min/pmol enzyme toward 22-hydroxydocosanoate(isoform CYP4F3B) {ECO:0000269|PubMed:18182499};Vmax=0.8 pmol/min/pmol enzyme toward 26-hydroxyhexacosanoate(isoform CYP4F3B) {ECO:0000269|PubMed:18182499};Note=The omega-hydroxylation of VLCFAs follows dual-enzymeMichaelis-Menten kinetics, suggesting simultaneous binding oftwo substrate molecules. The high affinity Michaelis-Mentenconstants are shown. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:16547005};pH dependence:Optimum pH is 7.5. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:9675028};PATHWAY: Lipid metabolism; leukotriene B4 degradation.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:9675028}.PATHWAY: Lipid metabolism; arachidonate metabolism.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:11461919}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Endoplasmic reticulum membrane{ECO:0000305|PubMed:10409674}; Single-pass membrane protein{ECO:0000305}. Microsome membrane {ECO:0000305|PubMed:10409674};Single-pass membrane protein {ECO:0000305}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative promoter usage, Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=CYP4F3A;IsoId=Q08477-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=CYP4F3B;IsoId=Q08477-2; Sequence=VSP_047193;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Isoform CYP4F3A is expressed in thepolymorphonuclear leukocytes as well as leukocytes and bonemarrow. Isoform CYP4F3B is selectively expressed in liver andkidney and is also the predominant CYP4F isoform in trachea andtissues of the gastrointestinal tract.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:11461919}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the cytochrome P450 family. {ECO:0000305}.WEB RESOURCE: Name=SeattleSNPs;URL=&quot;http://pga.gs.washington.edu/data/cyp4f3/&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
